"""RD04: native-BF16 flash-attn tile kernel series (net of 7 fork commits).

Provenance (group 'rdna-boosts' patches are external backports; the
machine-readable PROVENANCE dict below is cross-checked against
external-sources.toml by tools/tests/test_external_sources.py):

  source:            stew675-rdna-boosts
  repo:              https://github.com/stew675/llama.cpp
  locator:           rdna-boosts (branch name is a locator only, NOT identity)
  fork commits:      8623179e1, b619acd3c, 00b07f004, f18c14b10, cfc192734,
                     947070cf0, 0581c532c (contiguous in the branch; the v1
                     pre-rebase identity of the first commit is
                     cb05a6aec; the seven re-committed SHAs are the content
                     authorities)
                     "CUDA: read BF16 K/V natively in flash-attn tile kernel
                     with FP32 accumulation" + 6 follow-ups
  reviewed snapshot: v2 -- head 9e46e1fdc7a880f9ae9a2f9a693ae3e14c142a22
                     on base 4df29be4f4c3673f428170fda944a5b19f743bb8
  plan item:         RD04 (docs/planning/active/rdna-boost-experiments/RD04.md)
  mainline status:   NOT merged into ggml-org/llama.cpp master as of tip
                     6d0549831 (git cherry patch-id check, 2026-08-18)

What it does (performance + precision, kernel-level series):
  - the flash-attn TILE kernel reads BF16 K/V natively on RDNA3+ with FP32
    accumulation (the half2 F16 accumulators flush small values at deep
    context; fork: PPL 15.18 vs 15.59 F16 cache vs 14.97 F32 @ 32k)
  - Q is converted to BF16 at fill; KQ^T uses v_dot2_f32_bf16 (scalar FP32
    fallback elsewhere); standard 32-column configs apply again
  - packed BF16 PV (P rounded to BF16, v_perm_b32 row pairing,
    v_dot2_f32_bf16) is the only native-BF16 VKQ path, unconditional
  - all head sizes; the softmax KQ buffer is stored BF16 (halves SRAM);
    KQ_cs 8 to match the F16 kernel
  - non-RDNA3 targets keep the F16 tile path with BF16->F16 conversion
  - common.cuh: V_DOT2_F32_BF16 + the two ggml_cuda_mad/permutation helpers
  - tests: head 112 in the matrix, BF16 K/V for every head size

Porting notes:
  - GENERATED from the net diff 8623179e1^..0581c532c of the seven
    contiguous commits: the intermediate states cancel (the PV_DOT2 opt-in
    added in b619acd3c is removed in 00b07f004, etc.), so the patch ships
    only the net change as per-hunk replace edits. fattn-tile.cu /
    fattn-tile.cuh / fattn.cu are byte-identical between the pin and the
    fork pre-image (verified 2026-08-19); common.cuh and
    tests/test-backend-ops.cpp were hand-anchored against the base.
  - Base co-tenancy: fattn-* files have ZERO framework patches; common.cuh
    co-tenant 0900 is in a different region; the 1203/1204 (RD05-08)
    fattn.cu/fattn-mma-f16.cuh hunks are in different functions.

Isolation and promotion (first-sweep policy, RD review 2026-08-18):
  - GROUP 'rdna-boosts' + STATE 'untested' keeps this OUT of the
    production 'framework' and 'validated-enhancements' patch-sets.
  - Bench: BF16 KV-cache models, decode AND prefill at long context;
    PPL gate vs F16 (fork: +1.4% vs F32, i.e. BETTER than F16 cache);
    FLASH_ATTN_EXT must stay green.

Maintenance (future pin bumps / fork movement):
  - fattn-tile.cuh is heavily upstream-touched; re-derive the net diff
    from the tracked fork commits in external-sources.toml and run
    `python -m bigcherry sources check` before every pin bump.
"""

